text:
The DA RFOs in areas to be affected by TC “PAOLO”  have undertaken the following:
1. Activation of DA Regional DRRM Operations Centers;
2. Dissemination of advisories to concerned Local Government Units;
3. Positioning of seeds for rice, corn and high value crops; drugs and biologics for livestock and poultry; fish stocks and paraphernalia on fisheries;
4. Close coordination with RDRRMCs, LGUs and other concerned agencies in implementing preparedness measures on the impact of the TC;
5.  Monitoring of prices and movement of agricultural commodities; and
6. Allocation of funds for insurance and credit by the Philippine Crop Insurance Corporation and Agricultural Credit Policy Council (ACPC), respectively.
AVAILABLE INTERVENTIONS
In response to the needs of farmers and fisherfolk to be affected by the weather disturbance, the Department is ensuring that the following assistance are available:
1. Agricultural inputs such as rice, corn, and vegetable seeds, as well as livestock animals and biologics from DA RFOs;
2. Drugs and biologics for livestock and poultry;
3. Bags of rice stocks from the National Food Authority (NFA) for issuance to Local Government Units (LGUs) and other relief agencies;
4. Up to PhP 25,000 loanable amount from the Survival and Recovery (SURE) Loan Program of the Agricultural Credit Policy Council (ACPC), payable in three years at zero interest; and
5. Indemnification of insured affected farmers through the Philippine Crop Insurance Corporation (PCIC). The DA RFOs in areas to be affected by TC “PAOLO”  have undertaken the following: 1. Activation of DA Regional DRRM Operations Centers; 2. Dissemination of advisories to concerned Local Government Units; 3. Positioning of seeds for rice, corn and high value crops; drugs and biologics for livestock and poultry; fish stocks and paraphernalia on fisheries; 4. Close coordination with RDRRMCs, LGUs and other concerned agencies in implementing preparedness measures on the impact of the TC; 5.  Monitoring of prices and movement of agricultural commodities; and 6. Allocation of funds for insurance and credit by the Philippine Crop Insurance Corporation and Agricultural Credit Policy Council (ACPC), respectively. AVAILABLE INTERVENTIONS In response to the needs of farmers and fisherfolk to be affected by the weather disturbance, the Department is ensuring that the following assistance are available: 1. Agricultural inputs such as rice, corn, and vegetable seeds, as well as livestock animals and biologics from DA RFOs; 2. Drugs and biologics for livestock and poultry; 3. Bags of rice stocks from the National Food Authority (NFA) for issuance to Local Government Units (LGUs) and other relief agencies; 4. Up to PhP 25,000 loanable amount from the Survival and Recovery (SURE) Loan Program of the Agricultural Credit Policy Council (ACPC), payable in three years at zero interest; and 5. Indemnification of insured affected farmers through the Philippine Crop Insurance Corporation (PCIC). DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE
